{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Pushed for review: Gerrit change 2369\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2369 — `Split the git lock policy out of gitutil`\nChange-Id `Idbfc800e0b417fe1649d1edc94e235ab52fc9558`, commit `06b7b0a127673fb8a48777dc9513c1513608cef0`, rebased on `origin/main@4d1567206fb4`. Pushed for review only; NOT submitted. Worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/reb-2359-gitutil-split`, branch `split-gitutil-locking`.\n\n## Gate + prerequisite state\n\n- **file_impact: SET** (it was missing at ticket creation; the coverage gate would have flagged it). 10 paths declared in one `set-file-impact` call — the 2 source modules, the 7 retargeted test files, and `docs/concurrency.md`.\n- **plan-review: PASS, signed**, after 4 BLOCK rounds. Each blocker was a real gap in the plan prose, fixed rather than bypassed. No `--force` was used at any point.\n  1. AC claimed a RED->GREEN flip on the size test, but at 798/800 it is already GREEN. Reframed, with the measured boundary: 798 PASSES, 801 (three blank lines appended) FAILS, 373 PASSES.\n  2. Under-enumerated `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` importers. Re-derived by parsing import nodes rather than grepping: 6 importers, not the 3 originally listed.\n  3. Description exceeded the 8000-char admission cap (8080).\n  4. Omitted that `git_locking.py` must independently reconstruct `logger`, the `git_outcome` import, and the stdlib imports, since the moved bodies are byte-identical and read them as globals.\n- The first signed attestation went **stale** before the claim (`docs/concurrency.md` changed on `origin/main` mid-review). Re-ran the review and claimed back-to-back to close the window. Ticket is `in_progress`, assignee `joeoakhart@navapbc.com`.\n\n## Result\n\n`gitutil.py` 798 -> **373**; new `git_locking.py` **484**. Both inside the 200-500 target; ~427 lines of headroom instead of 2.\n\n## Behaviour-preservation evidence\n\n- `difflib` over the two moved line ranges vs the new module: the ONLY delta is two blank lines at the join. Every moved function body is byte-identical.\n- The retained half of `gitutil.py` differs from its pre-split content only in the docstring and import block. No executable line changed.\n- On the original base: the same 15 suites ran 194 passed + 1 failed (the failure being the module-size contract test) before, and 195 passed after — the single delta is the cap test. Broader run: 1408 passed, 9 skipped, 0 failed.\n- On the rebased base: `make lint` exit 0 (complexity ratchet `new=0 increased=0`), `make typecheck` exit 0 over 688 files, `check_comment_hygiene` / `check_raw_git_writes` / `check_wall_clock_asserts` clean, 254 targeted tests pass.\n- Every `rebar` module imports without error, so the re-exports hold for all production importers.\n\n## PER-PATCH EVIDENCE that the monkeypatch retargets are load-bearing\n\nThis is the part most likely to be silently wrong, so each site was proven, not asserted. 14 sites across 7 files were retargeted to `git_locking`.\n\n**Structural protection (6 of 7 moved names).** `_retry_probe`, `_reclaim_probe`, `_INDEX_LOCK_ATTEMPTS`, `_INDEX_LOCK_BACKOFF_S`, `_FETCH_COORD_WAIT_S`, `_FETCH_COORD_POLL_S` are deliberately NOT in `gitutil`'s re-export list. Since `monkeypatch.setattr` defaults to `raising=True`, a mis-target is a LOUD failure. Demonstrated by aiming each patch back at `gitutil` and running the owning suite:\n\n| file | mis-targeted name | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| test_compact_index_lock.py | `_retry_probe` | 2 failed, `AttributeError` |\n| test_delete_init_index_lock.py | `_retry_probe` | 3 failed, `AttributeError` |\n| test_event_append_index_lock.py | `_retry_probe` | 1 failed, `AttributeError` |\n| test_fsck_index_lock_reclaim_toctou.py | `_reclaim_probe` | 1 failed, `AttributeError` |\n| test_stale_lock_reclaim_write.py | `_reclaim_probe` | 1 failed, `AttributeError` |\n| test_git_contention_9305.py | `_INDEX_LOCK_ATTEMPTS` | 1 failed, `AttributeError` |\n| test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py | `_FETCH_COORD_WAIT_S` | 1 failed, `NameError` |\n\n**Seeded mutant (the ONE silently mis-targetable site).** `_backoff_sleep` IS re-exported on `gitutil` (its transient-fault retry reads it), so a mis-target there is vacuous rather than loud. For `test_uncontended_write_never_sleeps`, a `_backoff_sleep(0.001)` was seeded into the uncontended path of `_with_index_lock_retry`:\n- patched on `git_locking` (correct): **FAILS** — `AssertionError: uncontended happy path must not sleep, slept: [0.001]`\n- patched on `gitutil` (the old target), same mutant: **PASSES** — vacuous\nThat is the exact silent-failure mode, reproduced and closed.\n\n**Invocation probe (patches deliberately LEFT on `gitutil`).** `test_git_outcome.py` patches `\"rebar._store.gitutil._backoff_sleep\"` in string form; its reader `_with_transient_fault_retry` stayed in `gitutil`, so it must NOT be retargeted. Recording the calls: the `gitutil`-aimed patch **IS invoked**; the same probe aimed at `git_locking` is **never invoked** (fails). `gitutil.run_git` likewise stays — aiming it at `git_locking` gives 5 failures, `AttributeError`.\n\n**Honest non-claim.** Two seams are NOT module-sensitive: `gitutil.os` / `gitutil.subprocess` are the same stdlib module objects as `git_locking.os` / `.subprocess`, so patching either reaches the same object (verified `g.os is gl.os is os` -> True). The `git_locking.os` edit is a readability change, not a behavioural one, and I am not claiming proof for it.\n\n**`getattr` READ channel — a second vacuity path the reviewer caught.** `test_delete_init_index_lock.py:24` and `test_compact_index_lock.py:22` do `getattr(gitutil, \"_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S\", 300)`. This does NOT raise on a missing name, it falls through — and the real constant IS `300`, so comparing values proves nothing. Proven with a SENTINEL default: `getattr(gitutil, \"_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S\", sentinel) is not sentinel` -> True, and the value is the same object `git_locking` holds.\n\n## Next session\n\nWait for `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` on 2369, then Submit, then close this ticket. Do NOT close before the change merges."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787976640140834418,"uuid":"28fe0dde-604f-41eb-b7aa-81711bfbf22c"}